{
  "item": "kalnpc",
  "mu_name": "Oracle Layla",
  "mu_name_from": "NPC/kalnpc.bmd, loaded as MODEL_KALIMA_SHOP (ZzzOpenData.cpp:1994-1997, its textures out of Npc\\), MuMain's MONSTER_ORACLE_LAYLA, named KalimaShop (ZzzCharacter.cpp:14627-14632). Type 259, OpenMU's 'Oracle Layla' (VersionSeasonSix/NpcInitialization.cs:172), who stands in Kalima's base (KalimaBase.cs:34) and sells the potion girl's store (Updates/AddKalimaPlugIn.cs:59-64). Not Version075's.",
  "world": "losttower",
  "object_type": -1,
  "why_this_one": "The user asked for Layla as a figure for the Lost Tower's safe hall (2026-10-01); placement and her quest are the user's. A woman in a white robe with red vine paint, her potion bottles and a carved sandstone block with her: 1602 triangles on five sheets, 53 bones, one idle.",
  "profile": "npc",
  "sheets": {
    "npcl": "npc_npcl.png",
    "medicine1": "medicine1.png",
    "medicine2": "medicine2.png",
    "potion": "npc_potion.png",
    "ship": "npc_ship.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Out of Data/NPC, beside the model, decoded under an npc_ prefix. medicine1 and medicine2 decode pixel for pixel to the potions' own medicine1.png and medicine2.png already in source/textures, so they are shared.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "npcl": "skin",
    "medicine1": "glass",
    "medicine2": "glass",
    "potion": "glass",
    "ship": "rock"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "npcl is one page carrying her face and her robe together, so skin, as every townsperson's shared page does. medicine1 and medicine2 are the potions' glass, as Potion02's islands are; potion is a violet bottle with a gilt collar; ship is carved sandstone.",
  "placement_from": "CreateCharacter raises her: `c->Object.Position[2] += 140.0f` (ZzzCharacter.cpp:14630), 140 MU units (1.4 m) above the ground she is spawned on. Whoever stands her owes that lift; it is not in the mesh. Default scale, no subtype, no BlendMesh.",
  "draw_from": "RenderObjectMesh's MODEL_KALIMA_SHOP case (ZzzObject.cpp:1162-1198): every mesh RENDER_TEXTURE, opaque, under BodyLight (1,1,1), drawn in reverse order -- ship, potion, medicine2, medicine1, npcl -- which only matters to MU's own sorting; nothing is added or blended.",
  "effects_from": "Same case, not drawn yet: two BITMAP_LIGHT sprites in (0.4, 0.2, 0.4) violet, scale sin(WorldTime*0.002)*0.3+0.6 + 3.5, one at bone 3 (Bip01 Pelvis) offset (30, 40, 0) and one at bone 21 (Bip01 L Thigh); and BITMAP_SMOKE type 11 at 0.4 under her each frame (fps-checked), at (+40, +30, -90) and (-40, -30, -90) from her raised position.",
  "islands_from": "Found by the build, then assigned by sheet, the triangle counts adding up to export-obj's per mesh. 38 and 39 (432 + 38) are all of npcl, so skin. 0-37 (828) are medicine1 and medicine2 together, her rows of little bottles, glass as Potion02's are; 40-45 (192) are potion, the violet bottle, glass. 46 and 47 (102 + 10) are ship, the carved sandstone, rock.",
  "bake_share": {
    "medicine1": 0.03,
    "medicine2": 0.03,
    "potion": 0.2,
    "ship": 0.12
  },
  "bake_share_note": "Her bottles are the potions' 32-px and 16-px sheets drawn nineteen times over, the violet bottle's sheet four times, and the carved sandstone one 128 tile laid a dozen times round her seat; clean_lowpoly.match_density counted every repeat at full weight and left her robe and face 6% of the map. As Mace03's chain: the shares bring each repeated sheet back to about one sheet's room, so the page MU painted her on gets the most of it.",
  "obj_from": "tools/MuExtract export-obj and export-rig --actions=all off kalnpc.bmd, with one hand fix: the ship mesh carries two vertices no triangle uses (the 294th and 295th of its 310, OBJ 1599 and 1600), which Blender's OBJ import drops, and clean_lowpoly then refused the rig's 310 bindings against 308 vertices. Both are taken out of the .obj (faces renumbered) and out of the rig's ship vertex_bones (bone 50, as all of ship's are). Nothing drawn changes.",
